    "result_text": "All tests pass and the build succeeds. Let me summarize what I did.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe task: expose `telephoneDisplay` \u2014 the stored E.164 `telephone` formatted for humans (`+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`) \u2014 while keeping `telephone` as raw E.164.\n\nThe codebase's established pattern for derived read-only owner fields (`displayName`, `membershipNumber`, `locality`, etc.) is a **getter on the domain model** that MapStruct auto-maps to the OpenAPI-generated DTO. I followed that pattern rather than inventing a new path.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`model/Telephone.java` (new)** \u2014 a small final utility, matching the existing `Luhn`/`Regions` helper idiom, that holds the single source of truth for E.164 country knowledge (country code \u2192 required national length) and the `forDisplay(e164)` formatter (country code, space, national digits grouped in threes).\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added `getTelephoneDisplay()`, which delegates to `Telephone.forDisplay(telephone)`. The setter-free getter means MapStruct maps it to the DTO automatically, and reads it without touching the raw `telephone`.\n\n3. **`rest/validation/TelephoneNormalizer.java`** \u2014 refactored `requireValidNationalLength` to reuse `Telephone.countryCodeOf`/`nationalLength` and **deleted its private duplicate of the country-code table**. Now validation and display formatting share one table instead of copying it \u2014 no logic was moved into a catch-all, and the normalizer keeps only its parsing concerns.\n\n4. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `telephoneDisplay` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\nResult: the acceptance test `coreFormatsTelephoneDisplay` (input `0412 345 678` \u2192 `telephone` `+61412345678`, `telephoneDisplay` `+61 412 345 678`) passes, and the full suite is green.",
